  "summation": [
   {
    "dbId": 9933384,
    "displayName": "Both Retinoid-related orphan receptors (RORA, RORB, RORC) an...",
    "text": "Both Retinoid-related orphan receptors (RORA, RORB, RORC) and the heme-binding nuclear receptor NR1D1 (REV-ERBA) bind ROR response elements (RREs, ROREs) in DNA (reviewed in Duez and Staels 2008, Cox and Takahashi 2019, Laothamatas et al. 2023). RORs and NR1D1 produce opposite effects, however: RORs recruit coactivators such as EP300 (p300) and PPARGC1A to activate transcription; NR1D1 recruits the corepressor NCOR1 and the histone deacetylase HDAC3 to repress transcription.",
